501
00:49:25,098 --> 00:49:27,622
Yes, good, okay, good talk.   Yeah...

502
00:49:27,665 --> 00:49:31,854
I'll see you back at the house. Great. Thanks for stopping by and...

503
00:49:31,892 --> 00:49:34,039
the uh... breast hat.   I hope you like the, umm... the hat.

504
00:49:36,002 --> 00:49:38,222
Well, good night.

505
00:49:53,133 --> 00:49:55,501
Stay out of my way. I'm winning this thing!

506
00:49:55,585 --> 00:49:57,666
Good. Please. By all means.

507
00:50:10,602 --> 00:50:13,016
This time! This time for sure!

508
00:50:21,377 --> 00:50:25,639
No! No, sonofa half troll, rateating munch bucket...!

509
00:50:25,949 --> 00:50:26,962
Wait! Wait.

510
00:50:27,109 --> 00:50:28,130
So... later.

511
00:50:28,190 --> 00:50:30,673
Oh, oh! Not so fast!   I'm kinda late for...

512
00:50:30,963 --> 00:50:34,149
What! Late for what, exactly?

513
00:50:34,715 --> 00:50:37,493
Okay, quiet down. The Elder has decided.

514
00:50:49,192 --> 00:50:51,414
Boy, you've done it! You've done it, Hiccup!

515
00:50:51,630 --> 00:50:53,631
You get to kill the dragon!

516
00:50:56,442 --> 00:50:57,995
That's my boy!

517
00:50:58,132 --> 00:51:01,298
Yeah! Yes, I can't wait. I am so...

518
00:51:01,359 --> 00:51:03,506
leaving. We're Leaving.

519
00:51:03,542 --> 00:51:04,708
Let's pack up.

520
00:51:05,155 --> 00:51:07,735
Looks like you and me are taking a little vacation.

521
00:51:08,375 --> 00:51:09,417
Forever.

522
00:51:12,754 --> 00:51:14,125
Awww, man.

523
00:51:15,820 --> 00:51:19,423
What the...? Uh, w... what are you doing here?

524
00:51:20,047 --> 00:51:21,595
I want to know what's going on.

525
00:51:22,191 --> 00:51:24,644
No one just get as good as you do.

526
00:51:25,206 --> 00:51:26,752
Especially... you.

527
00:51:26,949 --> 00:51:28,617
Start talking.   I... I...

528
00:51:28,703 --> 00:51:29,610
Are you training with someone?

529
00:51:29,645 --> 00:51:30,832
Training? I didn't...

530
00:51:31,063 --> 00:51:32,743
It better not involve this.

531
00:51:32,824 --> 00:51:36,094
I know, this looks really bad but you see, this is...

532
00:51:38,985 --> 00:51:42,562
You're right. You're right. You're right. I... I'm through with the lies.

533
00:51:43,007 --> 00:51:45,107
I've been making... outfits!

534
00:51:45,256 --> 00:51:48,055
So, you got me. It's time everyone knew.

535
00:51:48,163 --> 00:51:50,454
Drag me back. Go ahead. Here we go.

536
00:51:50,812 --> 00:51:52,696
Oww. Why would you do that?

537
00:51:52,911 --> 00:51:54,423
That's for the lies!

538
00:51:54,695 --> 00:51:57,760
And that's... for everything else!

539
00:51:57,899 --> 00:51:58,884
Oh man.

540
00:51:59,778 --> 00:52:01,049
Get down!

541
00:52:02,772 --> 00:52:04,259
Run! Run!

542
00:52:05,145 --> 00:52:10,377
No! No! It's okay. It's okay. She's a friend.

543
00:52:12,875 --> 00:52:13,807
You just scared him.

544
00:52:13,827 --> 00:52:15,199
I scared him?

545
00:52:16,983 --> 00:52:18,689
Who is him?

546
00:52:19,360 --> 00:52:23,215
Astrid, Toothless. Toothless, Astrid.

547
00:52:28,969 --> 00:52:30,548
Dut, da da... We're dead.

548
00:52:32,069 --> 00:52:34,333
Woah, woah woah. Where do you think your going?

549
00:52:40,482 --> 00:52:43,113
Oh, great Odin! Don't. Oh, this is...

550
00:52:53,987 --> 00:52:56,608
Hiccup, get me down from here!

551
00:52:56,721 --> 00:52:58,794
You have to give me a chance to explain.

552
00:52:58,830 --> 00:53:01,901
I am not listening to anything you have to say!

553
00:53:01,947 --> 00:53:04,877
Then I won't speak. Just let me show you.

554
00:53:06,565 --> 00:53:07,944
Please, Astrid.

555
00:53:23,958 --> 00:53:25,511
Now get me down!

556
00:53:25,684 --> 00:53:28,373
Toothless, down. Gently.

557
00:53:30,043 --> 00:53:32,544
See, nothing to be afraid of.

558
00:53:36,067 --> 00:53:37,116
Toothless?

559
00:53:38,540 --> 00:53:41,131
What is wrong with you? Bad dragon!

560
00:53:42,161 --> 00:53:44,198
He's uh, he's not usually like this.

561
00:53:44,410 --> 00:53:45,363
Oh, no!

562
00:53:50,537 --> 00:53:52,925
Toothless, what are you doing? We need her to like us!

563
00:53:56,397 --> 00:53:58,513
And now he's spinning!

564
00:53:59,843 --> 00:54:02,097
Thank you for nothing you useless reptile!

565
00:54:03,601 --> 00:54:08,297
Okay, I am sorry, I'm sorry. Just get me off of this thing.

566
00:55:54,905 --> 00:55:57,865
Alright, I admit it. This is pretty cool.

567
00:55:59,133 --> 00:56:03,007
It's amazing. He's amazing.

568
00:56:05,932 --> 00:56:07,217
So what now?

569
00:56:08,546 --> 00:56:11,093
Hiccup, your final exam is tomorrow!

570
00:56:11,520 --> 00:56:13,105
You know your gonna have to kill a...

571
00:56:14,216 --> 00:56:15,033
kill a dragon...

572
00:56:15,241 --> 00:56:16,401
Don't remind me.

573
00:56:18,376 --> 00:56:19,673
Toothless, what happening?

574
00:56:21,799 --> 00:56:23,362
Whoa, what is it?

575
00:56:26,435 --> 00:56:27,575
Get down!

576
00:56:44,818 --> 00:56:46,782
What's going on?   I don't know.

577
00:56:46,870 --> 00:56:49,555
Toothless, you gotta get us out of here, bud.

578
00:56:52,337 --> 00:56:54,912
It looks like they're hauling in their kill.

579
00:56:55,828 --> 00:56:57,570
What does that make us?

580
00:57:40,933 --> 00:57:43,694
What my dad wouldn't give to find this.

581
00:57:59,805 --> 00:58:03,745
Oh, it's satisfying to know that all of our food has been dumped down a hole.

582
00:58:04,771 --> 00:58:06,636
They're not eating any of it.

583
00:58:21,714 --> 00:58:23,386
What... was that?

584
00:58:30,820 --> 00:58:33,479
Alright, bud, we gotta get out of here. Now!

585
00:58:43,122 --> 00:58:46,427
No, no, it totally makes sense. It's like a giant beehive.

586
00:58:46,775 --> 00:58:48,960
They're the workers, and that's their queen.

587
00:58:49,026 --> 00:58:51,928
It controls them. Let's find your dad.

588
00:58:51,965 --> 00:58:53,095
No, no.

589
00:58:53,895 --> 00:58:57,169
No. Not yet. They'll kill Toothless.

590
00:58:57,700 --> 00:58:59,724
Astrid, we have to think this through, carefully.

591
00:59:00,681 --> 00:59:03,762
Hiccup, we just discovered the dragon's nest.

592
00:59:03,845 --> 00:59:06,793
The thing we've been after since Vikings first sailed here.

593
00:59:06,984 --> 00:59:08,657
And you want to keep it secret?

594
00:59:08,977 --> 00:59:12,003
To protect your pet, dragon? Are you serious?

595
00:59:14,529 --> 00:59:15,658
Yes.

596
00:59:23,196 --> 00:59:25,226
Okay. Then what do we do?

597
00:59:25,680 --> 00:59:29,250
Just give me until tomorrow. I'll figure something out.

598
00:59:30,229 --> 00:59:31,287
Okay...

599
00:59:32,506 --> 00:59:34,000
That's for kidnapping me.

600
00:59:40,999 --> 00:59:43,667
That's for... everything else.

601
00:59:52,722 --> 00:59:54,450
What are you looking at?

602
00:59:59,300 --> 01:00:02,081
Well, I can show my face in public again.

603
01:00:04,973 --> 01:00:08,135
If someone had told me that in a few short weeks

604
01:00:08,520 --> 01:00:15,638
Hiccup will go from... well being... uh... Hiccup,

605
01:00:16,037 --> 01:00:18,991
to placing first in dragon training.

606
01:00:19,119 --> 01:00:23,579
Well, I would have tied him to a mast and shipped him off. For fear he'd gone mad.

607
01:00:24,753 --> 01:00:26,097
And you know it.

608
01:00:27,449 --> 01:00:29,428
But, here we are.

609
01:00:30,007 --> 01:00:35,027
And no ones more surprised or more proud than I am.

610
01:00:36,121 --> 01:00:39,178
Today my boy becomes a Viking!

611
01:00:40,082 --> 01:00:43,231
Today he becomes one of us!

612
01:00:47,207 --> 01:00:49,018
Be careful with that dragon.

613
01:00:49,054 --> 01:00:50,843
It's not the dragon I'm worried about.

614
01:00:51,158 --> 01:00:52,455
What are you going to do?

615
01:00:52,601 --> 01:00:54,045
Put an end to this.

616
01:00:54,491 --> 01:00:55,747
I have to try.

617
01:00:56,314 --> 01:01:01,719
Astrid, if something goes wrong, just make sure they don't find Toothless.

618
01:01:02,292 --> 01:01:05,911
I will, just promise me it won't go wrong.

619
01:01:06,939 --> 01:01:08,138
It's time, Hiccup.

620
01:01:08,705 --> 01:01:10,143
Knock 'em dead.

621
01:01:33,703 --> 01:01:35,711
I'd have gone for the hammer.

622
01:01:39,593 --> 01:01:41,005
I'm ready.

623
01:02:05,524 --> 01:02:08,116
Go on Hiccup, give it to him!

624
01:02:11,904 --> 01:02:13,453
What is he doing?

625
01:02:16,335 --> 01:02:18,646
It's okay, it's okay.

626
01:02:26,704 --> 01:02:28,280
I'm not one of them.

627
01:02:32,869 --> 01:02:34,684
What's he thinking?

628
01:02:34,721 --> 01:02:35,877
Stop the fight!

629
01:02:36,179 --> 01:02:38,688
No! I need you all to see this.

630
01:02:40,141 --> 01:02:42,400
They're not what we think they are.

631
01:02:42,893 --> 01:02:44,519
We don't have to kill them.

632
01:02:46,085 --> 01:02:48,296
I said stop the fight!

633
01:02:56,209 --> 01:02:57,145
Out of my way!

634
01:02:57,182 --> 01:02:58,166
Hiccup!

635
01:03:19,380 --> 01:03:20,396
Hiccup!

636
01:03:26,810 --> 01:03:27,813
This way!

637
01:03:48,555 --> 01:03:49,946
Night Fury!

638
01:04:08,246 --> 01:04:10,203
Alright, Toothless. Go! Get out of here.

639
01:04:12,561 --> 01:04:13,961
Go, go!

640
01:04:14,321 --> 01:04:16,333
No, dad! Dad, he won't hurt you!

641
01:04:21,229 --> 01:04:22,566
Toothless, stop!

642
01:04:24,209 --> 01:04:26,186
No. No!

643
01:04:30,016 --> 01:04:31,496
Get him!

644
01:04:34,687 --> 01:04:36,397
No, no, please. Just don't hurt him

645
01:04:37,434 --> 01:04:38,730
Please. Don't hurt him

646
01:04:45,525 --> 01:04:47,366
Put it with the others.

647
01:04:49,813 --> 01:04:51,118
I should have known.

648
01:04:51,487 --> 01:04:52,890
I should have seen the signs.

649
01:04:52,974 --> 01:04:54,647
Dad?   We had a deal!

650
01:04:54,776 --> 01:04:58,719
I know! We did, but that was before I... Oh, it's all so messed up.

651
01:04:58,848 --> 01:05:02,178
So everything in that ring... A trick? A lie?

652
01:05:02,515 --> 01:05:05,117
I screwed up. I should have told you before now.

653
01:05:06,201 --> 01:05:10,515
Take this out on me, be mad at me, but please, just don't hurt Toothless.

654
01:05:10,891 --> 01:05:13,578
The dragon? That's what you're worried about?

655
01:05:14,036 --> 01:05:15,658
Not the people you almost killed?

656
01:05:15,690 --> 01:05:17,840
He was just protecting me! He's not dangerous.

657
01:05:18,234 --> 01:05:20,375
They've killed hundreds of us!

658
01:05:20,472 --> 01:05:24,745
And we've killed thousands of them. They defend themselves, that's all.

659
01:05:25,753 --> 01:05:27,678
They raid us because they have to.

660
01:05:28,132 --> 01:05:31,752
If they don't bring enough food back, they'll be eaten themselves.

661
01:05:32,099 --> 01:05:35,872
There's something else on their island, dad. It's a dragonlike...

662
01:05:36,244 --> 01:05:39,460
Their island? So, you've been to the nest?

663
01:05:39,612 --> 01:05:41,567
Did I say nest?   How did you find it?

664
01:05:41,602 --> 01:05:46,540
No, no, I didn't. Toothless did. Only a dragon can find the island.

665
01:05:48,238 --> 01:05:51,066
No, no, dad, no please. It's not what you think.

666
01:05:51,244 --> 01:05:54,360
You don't know what your up against. It's like nothing you've ever seen.

667
01:05:54,944 --> 01:05:57,890
Dad, please, I promise you. You can't win this one!

668
01:05:58,660 --> 01:06:00,074
Dad, no!

669
01:06:00,500 --> 01:06:03,506
For once in your life, would you please just listen to me!

670
01:06:07,269 --> 01:06:09,165
You've thrown your lot in with them.

671
01:06:09,864 --> 01:06:11,440
You're not a Viking.

672
01:06:13,212 --> 01:06:14,976
You're not my son!

673
01:06:18,682 --> 01:06:20,277
Ready the ships!

674
01:07:15,255 --> 01:07:16,556
Set sail!

675
01:07:16,676 --> 01:07:18,804
We head for Hell Hounds gate.

676
01:07:27,225 --> 01:07:29,718
Lead us home, devil.

677
01:07:50,682 --> 01:07:54,925
It's a mess. You must feel horrible.

678
01:07:55,511 --> 01:08:00,047
You've lost everything. Your father, your tribe, your best friend.

679
01:08:00,267 --> 01:08:02,166
Thank you for summing that up.

680
01:08:04,247 --> 01:08:07,057
Why couldn't I've killed that dragon, when I found him the woods?

681
01:08:07,933 --> 01:08:09,725
Would've been better for everyone.

682
01:08:09,874 --> 01:08:11,551
Yep, the rest of us would have done it.

683
01:08:12,992 --> 01:08:14,617
So, why didn't you?

684
01:08:17,513 --> 01:08:18,911
Why didn't you?

685
01:08:19,505 --> 01:08:21,976
I don't know. I couldn't.

686
01:08:22,140 --> 01:08:25,489
That's not an answer.   Why is this so important to you all of a sudden?

687
01:08:25,909 --> 01:08:29,227
Because I want to remember what you say, right now.

688
01:08:29,279 --> 01:08:32,651
Ah, for the love of... I was coward, I was weak.

689
01:08:33,043 --> 01:08:34,588
I wouldn't kill a dragon!

690
01:08:34,654 --> 01:08:35,900
You said wouldn't that time?

691
01:08:35,969 --> 01:08:37,935
Whatever, I wouldn't!

692
01:08:38,653 --> 01:08:42,138
300 years and I'm the first Viking who wouldn't kill a dragon.

693
01:08:46,248 --> 01:08:48,470
First to ride one though.

694
01:08:51,067 --> 01:08:52,017
So?

695
01:08:54,869 --> 01:08:58,098
I wouldn't kill him because he looked as frightened as I was.

696
01:08:59,168 --> 01:09:02,674
I looked at him and I saw myself.

697
01:09:04,820 --> 01:09:06,809
I bet he's really frightened now.

698
01:09:07,514 --> 01:09:09,141
What are you gonna do about it?

699
01:09:10,659 --> 01:09:13,378
Probably something stupid.

700
01:09:13,724 --> 01:09:15,647
Good, but you've already done that.

701
01:09:17,112 --> 01:09:18,866
Then something crazy!

702
01:09:20,155 --> 01:09:21,920
That's more like it.

703
01:09:30,689 --> 01:09:34,043
Sound your positions! Stay within earshot.

704
01:09:36,911 --> 01:09:41,390
Listen, Stoick, I was overhearing some of the men just now and well, you know...

705
01:09:41,422 --> 01:09:44,151
some of them are wondering what it is we're up to here?

706
01:09:44,262 --> 01:09:47,594
Not me of course. I know you are always the man with the plan.

707
01:09:47,720 --> 01:09:52,069
But some, not me, are wondering if there is in fact a plan at all...

708
01:09:52,438 --> 01:09:54,314
and what it might be?

709
01:09:54,420 --> 01:09:56,132
Find the nest and take it.

710
01:09:56,390 --> 01:10:00,784
Of course. Send them running. The old Viking fallback. Nice and simple.

711
01:10:09,330 --> 01:10:10,610
Step aside.

712
01:10:24,102 --> 01:10:25,797
Head to port.

713
01:10:30,420 --> 01:10:36,126
If you're planning on getting eaten, I'd definitely go with the Gronckle.

714
01:10:37,369 --> 01:10:41,401
You were wise to seek help from the world's most deadly weapon.

715
01:10:41,727 --> 01:10:42,362
It's me.

716
01:10:42,396 --> 01:10:44,761
I love this plan!   I didn't...

717
01:10:44,817 --> 01:10:47,634
You're crazy. I like that.

718
01:10:48,747 --> 01:10:51,109
So, what is the plan?

719
01:11:00,812 --> 01:11:03,021
That's not very encouraging.

720
01:11:03,336 --> 01:11:06,859
Oh, I was wondering where that went.

721
01:11:19,631 --> 01:11:22,146
Stay low, and ready your weapons.

722
01:11:38,676 --> 01:11:39,990
We're here.

723
01:12:12,432 --> 01:12:13,963
Wait, what are you... ?!

724
01:12:15,245 --> 01:12:17,678
It's okay... It's okay.

725
01:12:29,078 --> 01:12:30,183
Where are you going?

726
01:12:30,237 --> 01:12:33,069
You're gonna need something to help you hold on.

727
01:12:41,961 --> 01:12:46,334
When we crack this mountain open, all hell is gonna break loose.

728
01:12:46,341 --> 01:12:49,057
In my undies. Good thing I brought extras.

729
01:12:49,512 --> 01:12:52,599
No matter how this ends, it ends today.

730
01:13:48,273 --> 01:13:50,087
Is that it?

731
01:13:53,848 --> 01:13:56,379
We've done it!

732
01:14:04,202 --> 01:14:05,447
This isn't over!

733
01:14:05,677 --> 01:14:07,931
Form your ranks. Pull together!

734
01:14:21,627 --> 01:14:23,054
Get clear!

735
01:14:33,044 --> 01:14:35,705
Beards of Thor...! What is that?

736
01:14:39,943 --> 01:14:41,688
Odin, help us!

737
01:14:46,396 --> 01:14:48,578
Catapults!   Fire!

738
01:14:57,311 --> 01:14:59,616
Get to the ships!   No, nooo!

739
01:15:12,573 --> 01:15:14,568
Not that one...   I was a fool.

740
01:15:14,654 --> 01:15:16,790
Lead the men to the far side of the island.

741
01:15:17,171 --> 01:15:18,167
Gobber, go with the men.

742
01:15:18,228 --> 01:15:21,219
I think I'll stay, just in case you're thinking of doing something crazy.

743
01:15:21,273 --> 01:15:24,497
I can buy them a few minutes if I give that thing something to hunt for.

744
01:15:24,895 --> 01:15:27,310
Then I can double that time.

745
01:15:28,399 --> 01:15:31,978
Here!   Oh, no. Here!

746
01:15:43,634 --> 01:15:46,652
Fight me!   No, me!

747
01:15:53,687 --> 01:15:55,620
Ruff, Tuff, watch your backs!

748
01:15:56,377 --> 01:15:57,409
Move, Fishlegs!

749
01:15:58,547 --> 01:16:02,388
Look at us! We're on dragons! We're on dragons! All of us!

750
01:16:06,814 --> 01:16:11,203
Every bit the bullheaded stubborn Viking you ever were.

751
01:16:12,971 --> 01:16:14,607
Fishlegs, break it down!   Okay.

752
01:16:15,017 --> 01:16:18,725
Heavily armored skull and tail made for bashing and crushing. Steer clear of both.

753
01:16:18,812 --> 01:16:22,192
Small eyes, large nostrils. Relies on hearing and smell.

754
01:16:22,218 --> 01:16:26,274
Okay, Lout, Legs, hang in its blind spot. Make some noise. Keep it confused.

755
01:16:26,302 --> 01:16:29,304
Ruff, Tuff, find out if it has a shot limit. Make it mad.

756
01:16:29,854 --> 01:16:31,799
That's my specialty!   Since when?

757
01:16:31,852 --> 01:16:33,678
Everyone knows I'm more irritating, see.

758
01:16:34,805 --> 01:16:37,560
Just do what I told you. I'll be back as soon as I can.

759
01:16:38,378 --> 01:16:39,984
Don't worry! We got it covered!

760
01:16:40,026 --> 01:16:41,236
Yeah!

761
01:16:49,048 --> 01:16:50,345
Fool!   Butto!

762
01:16:50,377 --> 01:16:51,704
Bye, ya Grendel!

763
01:16:57,954 --> 01:17:00,335
Um, this thing doesn't have a blind spot!

764
01:17:02,882 --> 01:17:04,101
There!

765
01:17:13,026 --> 01:17:14,166
Go help the others!

766
01:17:15,658 --> 01:17:16,706
Okay, hold on. Hold on.

767
01:17:21,079 --> 01:17:23,714
It's working!   Yeah, it's working!

768
01:17:33,630 --> 01:17:37,358
I've lost power on the Gronckle! Snotlout, do something!

769
01:17:39,773 --> 01:17:40,680
I'm okay!

770
01:17:41,537 --> 01:17:42,982
Less okay.

771
01:17:45,994 --> 01:17:49,555
I can't miss! What's wrong, buddy? You got something in your eye?

772
01:17:53,472 --> 01:17:55,439
Yeah, you're the Viking!

773
01:18:01,397 --> 01:18:02,303
Woah!

774
01:18:33,157 --> 01:18:34,417
Dad?

775
01:18:53,563 --> 01:18:54,681
You got it, buddy!

776
01:18:56,743 --> 01:18:57,541
Hiccup!

777
01:19:00,365 --> 01:19:01,056
I'm sorry...

778
01:19:02,398 --> 01:19:03,583
for... for everything.

779
01:19:04,331 --> 01:19:05,523
Yeah... me too.

780
01:19:05,560 --> 01:19:07,148
You don't have to go up there.

781
01:19:08,142 --> 01:19:11,260
We're Vikings. It's an occupational hazard...

782
01:19:12,456 --> 01:19:15,016
I'm proud to call you my son.

783
01:19:17,013 --> 01:19:18,388
Thanks, Dad.

784
01:19:24,208 --> 01:19:25,140
He's up!

785
01:19:28,876 --> 01:19:30,285
Get Snotlout outta there!

786
01:19:30,390 --> 01:19:31,603
I'm on it!   I'm on it first!

787
01:19:31,706 --> 01:19:33,825
Hey, let me drive!

788
01:19:34,831 --> 01:19:36,855
Don't push me!   I'll push your teeth out!

789
01:19:40,541 --> 01:19:42,243
You know, I can't believe that worked.

790
01:19:50,376 --> 01:19:52,943
Night Fury!   Get down!

791
01:20:03,827 --> 01:20:04,821
Did you get her?

792
01:20:14,750 --> 01:20:15,332
Go!

793
01:20:15,700 --> 01:20:20,121
This thing has wings. Okay, let's see if it can use them!

794
01:20:36,484 --> 01:20:37,955
You think that did it?

795
01:20:43,525 --> 01:20:44,862
Well, he can fly.

796
01:21:06,048 --> 01:21:10,209
Okay, Toothless, time to disappear! Come on, bud!

797
01:21:16,576 --> 01:21:17,946
Here it comes!

798
01:22:09,988 --> 01:22:11,121
Watch out!

799
01:22:13,292 --> 01:22:15,961
Okay, time's up. Let's see if this works.

800
01:22:18,948 --> 01:22:20,955
Come on! Is that the best you can do?

801
01:22:38,788 --> 01:22:41,442
Stay with me, buddy. We're good. Just a little bit longer.

802
01:22:46,083 --> 01:22:49,576
Hold, Toothless. Now!

803
01:23:13,374 --> 01:23:15,968
No... No!

804
01:23:32,243 --> 01:23:35,988
Hiccup! Hiccup!

805
01:23:37,776 --> 01:23:38,866
Son!

806
01:23:41,632 --> 01:23:42,596
Hiccup!

807
01:24:04,121 --> 01:24:05,367
Oh son!

808
01:24:07,274 --> 01:24:08,619
I did this.

809
01:24:39,159 --> 01:24:42,940
I'm s... I'm so sorry.

810
01:24:48,789 --> 01:24:49,808
Hiccup!

811
01:24:56,578 --> 01:24:59,947
He's alive! You brought him back alive!

812
01:25:16,851 --> 01:25:19,895
Thank you... for saving my son.

813
01:25:20,707 --> 01:25:23,966
Well, you know, most of him.

814
01:25:41,923 --> 01:25:43,422
Hey, Toothless.

815
01:25:44,632 --> 01:25:46,476
Happy to see you too, buddy.

816
01:25:47,170 --> 01:25:51,702
Aawww, what... uh... I'm... in my house

817
01:25:53,489 --> 01:25:54,824
You're in my house.

818
01:25:55,732 --> 01:25:57,296
Does my dad know you're here?

819
01:25:57,467 --> 01:25:59,409
Uh, what, oh, okay... okay.

820
01:26:00,531 --> 01:26:04,162
Toothless, no. Toothless! Aw, come on.

821
01:26:42,543 --> 01:26:44,844
Okay. Thanks, bud.

822
01:26:55,925 --> 01:26:57,760
Toothless, stay here.

823
01:26:58,178 --> 01:27:01,268
C'mon guys. Get ready! Hold on tight. Here we go!

824
01:27:03,866 --> 01:27:05,066
What?

825
01:27:13,942 --> 01:27:16,026
I knew it. I'm dead.

826
01:27:16,921 --> 01:27:19,026
No, but you give it your best shot.

827
01:27:19,116 --> 01:27:21,016
So, what do you think?

828
01:27:21,045 --> 01:27:22,672
Hey look, it's Hiccup!

829
01:27:24,446 --> 01:27:25,115
Hiccup!

830
01:27:27,339 --> 01:27:31,357
It turns out, all we needed was a little more of... this.

831
01:27:31,704 --> 01:27:33,600
You just gestured to all of me?

832
01:27:34,566 --> 01:27:38,005
Well, most of you. That bit's my handiwork.

833
01:27:38,113 --> 01:27:41,515
With a little Hiccup flare thrown in. You think that'll do?

834
01:27:41,954 --> 01:27:43,887
I might make a few tweaks.

835
01:27:45,296 --> 01:27:47,582
That's... for scaring me.

836
01:27:47,684 --> 01:27:50,084
What... what, is it always going to be this way? Because...

837
01:27:53,181 --> 01:27:54,567
I could get used to it.

838
01:27:57,833 --> 01:27:59,423
Welcome home.

839
01:27:59,663 --> 01:28:01,873
Night Fury!   Get down!

840
01:28:13,360 --> 01:28:14,682
You ready?

841
01:28:17,170 --> 01:28:18,978
This is Berk...

842
01:28:19,771 --> 01:28:23,694
It snows nine months of the year and hails the other three.

843
01:28:25,340 --> 01:28:28,204
Any food that grows here is tough and tasteless.

844
01:28:30,599 --> 01:28:33,496
The people that grow here are even more so.

845
01:28:37,281 --> 01:28:39,982
The only upsides are the pets.

846
01:28:42,756 --> 01:28:45,977
While other places have ponies or parrots...

847
01:28:47,900 --> 01:28:49,099
We have...

848
01:28:50,350 --> 01:28:52,003
Dragons.

